WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Many time problems are system problems rather than character flaws.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:12.611
Overcommitment often comes from unclear priorities, hidden work, optimistic estimates, and a culture that rewards saying yes.

3
00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:18.049
Meeting overload can grow because meetings are the default coordination mechanism.

4
00:00:18.049 --> 00:00:24.090
Constant availability can appear helpful while making focused execution nearly impossible.

5
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.225
When a system spends time badly, individual willpower is not enough to repair it.

6
00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:32.170
Multitasking is another common failure mode.

7
00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:38.816
People can switch quickly between tasks, but demanding work still pays a cost when attention fragments.

8
00:00:38.816 --> 00:00:45.537
A person may feel busy all day while never staying with one important problem long enough to make progress.

9
00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:48.708
Busyness is visible and often socially rewarded.

10
00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:49.841
Value is quieter.

11
00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:55.958
It shows up in decisions made, work completed, risks reduced, and relationships strengthened.

12
00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:59.734
Perfectionism and procrastination can both distort time.

13
00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:06.077
Perfectionism keeps effort locked on diminishing returns when useful completion would be enough.

14
00:01:06.077 --> 00:01:11.439
Procrastination delays the uncomfortable start until urgency supplies pressure.

15
00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:18.311
All-or-nothing planning adds another trap: if the ideal plan breaks, the person abandons the whole system.

16
00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:24.277
A resilient time system expects imperfection and gives people a way to restart without drama.

17
00:01:24.277 --> 00:01:28.204
Ignoring recovery is one of the most expensive failure modes.

18
00:01:28.204 --> 00:01:37.719
Sustainable performance requires attention, energy, and judgment, and those are affected by rest, transitions, boundaries, and reasonable load.

19
00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:44.289
This course is not giving medical advice, but it is practical to recognize that people are not machines.

20
00:01:44.289 --> 00:01:53.351
A system that consumes recovery may look productive briefly, then pay for it through errors, conflict, rework, and lower-quality decisions.
